# A narrow heater on a slab over a heat sink: the surface temperature is P / (pi k) ln coth(pi x / (4 d)), and far away it decays as exp(-pi x / (2 d)).
# Reference: that closed form, within 3% (6% at the farthest probe) for a heater two cells wide.
title Line heater on a 3 um slab of conductivity 0.2
grid dx=0.125 dy=0.125
window width=48 ymin=-3 ymax=0
material slab k=0.2 c=1.6e6
background slab
heater h xmin=-0.125 xmax=0.125 ymin=-0.125 ymax=0 power=0.1
probe p0 x=1.5625 y=-0.0625
probe p1 x=3.0625 y=-0.0625
probe p2 x=6.0625 y=-0.0625
probe p3 x=9.0625 y=-0.0625
expect response p0 h 1507.54248 1e-7
expect response p1 h 649.123759 1e-7
expect response p2 h 133.236995 1e-7
expect response p3 h 27.696976 1e-7
expect peak 597.005654 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 9216
expect response p0 h 1508.13 0.03
expect response p1 h 649.254 0.03
expect response p2 h 133.203 0.03
expect response p3 h 27.6748 0.06
expect crosstalk p3 p2 h 0.20788 0.05
